    "product_id": "6af0ea46-fd53-4e07-b826-2b4469906323",
    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 010723\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n1223 AM PDT Thu Oct 1 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Above-normal temperatures and quiet conditions continue into\n  next week as high pressure dominates.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...through Wednesday.\n\nEnsemble guidances is in good agreement on the development of a \nridge over the southwestern US today and sticking around through at \nleast the middle of next week. This feature will promote anomalously \nwarm temperatures, with forecast highs up to 10 degrees above normal \nat times. However, heat risk during this time largely remains in the \nminor category, with just Death Valley in the moderate to major \ncategories. A weak disturbance passing through on Sunday and Monday \ntries to spur a slight uptick in winds and minor cooling, but \nimpacts are not expected. Precipitation chances stay below 5% across \nthe entire area.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 06Z Forecast Package... \nFairly benign weather expected through the rest of the TAF period. \nLight SW winds this evening become light and variable into the \novernight hours. By 18z Thursday, expect a E-NE wind to set up \naround 8 kts, potentially becoming ESE into the evening. Winds \nbecome light and variable again after sunset. No cig or vis issues \nexpected. \n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 06Z Forecast Package...Winds will remain around \n5-10KT across the region the next 24 hours, following typical daily \ndirectional patterns with some variability. For KDAG, Light west \nwinds tonight become variable in the afternoon, favoring an E-NE \ndirection. KBIH may observe isolated southerly wind gusts around 15 \nkt during peak heating of the day tomorrow, diminishing after \nsunset. VFR conditions with clear skies continue. \n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Woods\nAVIATION...Moore\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
